G1839.def:
ἐξ-ίστημι (also in Hellenistic -ιστάνω, Act 8:9), 
[in LXX for H2730, etc. (29 words in all) ;], 
__1. causal in Pres., impf., fut., 1 aor., to put out of its place; metaphorically, ἐ. τινά φρενῶν (Eur.), to drive one out of his senses, hence, absol., to confound, amaze: with accusative of person(s), Luc 24:22, Actes 8:9, 11. 
__2. Intr. in pass. and mid., also in 2 aor., pf., plpf. act., before ἐκ or with genitive, to stand aside from, retire from; esp. τ. φρενῶν, to lose one's senses (Eur.), hence, absol.; 
__(a) to be beside oneself, be mad: Marc 3:21, 2 Corinthiens 5:13 (opposite to σωφρονεῖν); 
__(b) to be amazed, confounded: Matthieu 12:23, Marc 2:12 Marc 5:42 Marc 6:51, Luc 2:47 Luc 8:56, Actes 2:7, 12 Actes 8:13 Actes 9:21 Actes 10:45 Actes 12:16 (Cremer, 309).†

G1854.def:
ἔξω 
adv. (ἐξ), [in LXX for חוּץ ;] 
__1. outside, without; 
__(a) adverbially: Matthieu 12:46, Marc 3:31 11:4, Luc 8:20, Jean 18:16, al.; with art., ὁ ἔ., he who is without; metaphorically, in pl., οἱ ἔ., of those outside the Church, 1 Corinthiens 5:12-13, Colossiens 4:5 (Lft., in l), 1 Thessaloniciens 4:12; ὁ ἔ. ἄνθρωπος, 2 Corinthiens 4:16; αἱ ἔ. πόλεις, Actes 26:11; 
__(b) as prep. with genitive: Luc 13:33, Actes 21:5, Hébreux 13:11-12 
__2. After verbs of motion; 
__(a) adverbially, forth, out: Matthieu 5:13 Marc 14:68, Luc 22:62, Jean 19:4, 13, Actes 9:40, al.; 
__(b) as prep. with genitive, out of: Matthieu 21:17, Marc 11:19 12:8, Luc 4:29, Actes 7:58, Hébreux 13:13, al

G1861.def:
ἐπ-αγγέλλω 
[in LXX: Esther 4:8 (אָמַר), Proverbes 13:12, Wis.2:13, al. ;] 
__1. to announce, proclaim. 
__2. (a) to promise; 
__(b) to profess. Mid., also frequently in both these senses; 
__(with) to promise: with dab. of person(s), Hébreux 6:13; with accusative of thing(s), Romains 4:21, Tite 1:2; with dative of person(s) and accusative of thing(s), Jacques 1:12 2:5, 2 Pierre 2:19; ἐπαγγελίαν, 1 Jean 2:25; with inf., Marc 14:11, Actes 7:5; before λέγων, Hébreux 12:26; ptcp., Hébreux 10:23 11:11; 
__(d) to profess: θεοσέβειαν, 1 Timothée 2:10; γνῶσιν, 1 Timothée 6:21. Pass., Galates 3:19 (cf. προ-επαγγέλλω; and see Cremer, 26).†

G1864.def:
ἐπ-αγωνίζομαι depon.; 
__1. to contend with (Plut.). 
__2. to contend for (C.I., 2335, 19): with dative of thing(s), Ju 3.†

G1883.def:
ἐπ-άνω 
adv., [in LXX for מַעֲלָה, עַל, מֵעָל, etc. ;] 
above; 
__1. adverbially; 
__(a) of place: Luc 11:44; 
__(b) of number, more than: Marc 14:5, 1 Corinthiens 15:6. 
__2. As prep. C. genitive; 
__(a) of place: Matthieu 2:9 5:14 21:7 23:18-22 27:37 28:2, Luc 4:39 10:19, Apocalypse 6:8 20:3; 
__(b) of pre-eminence: Luc 19:17-19, Jean 3:31.†
